e for about 5 weeks, peaking at $113.50 and pulling back 18% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Mar 23, 2026 it closed at $114.43, its first close above the base high of $113.50. Volume that day was 5.9M shares, 1.20x the prior 10-day average of 4.9M. It didn't hold. By Apr 13, 2026 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $153.01.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}